IELTS.lesson({"test": 2, "part": 3, "title": "Test 2, Part 3 — the discussion", "candidate": "hadi", "script": [{"who": "examiner", "text": "We've been talking about a skill you learned that was difficult at first, and I'd like to discuss with you one or two more general questions related to this.", "ar": "كنّا نتحدّث عن مهارة تعلّمتها وكانت صعبة في البداية، وأودّ أن أناقش معك سؤالاً أو سؤالين أعمّ تتعلّق بهذا الموضوع.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/392382fbcf47b537.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Let's consider learning at work.", "ar": "لننظر في التعلّم في العمل.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/58f5ab89963e0e6b.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do people learn more from training courses or from experience at work?", "ar": "هل يتعلّم الناس أكثر من الدورات التدريبية أم من الخبرة في العمل؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/e547c759604bc219.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Experience, I'd say, for the kind of work I do. A course gives you the rules, which you need, and I'm not against them. But a course can't give you the feeling that something's wrong before you can say why, and on a site in Homs that feeling is most of the job.", "ar": "الخبرة، على ما أعتقد، لنوع العمل الذي أقوم به. الدورة تعطيك القواعد، وأنت بحاجة إليها، ولست ضدّها. لكن الدورة لا تستطيع أن تمنحك الإحساس بأن شيئاً ما خطأ قبل أن تستطيع أن تقول لماذا، وفي موقع في حمص ذلك الإحساس هو معظم العمل.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/289e4fc5d947d30c.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Should companies be responsible for training their workers?", "ar": "هل يجب أن تكون الشركات مسؤولة عن تدريب عامليها؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/2d47604312e41ddd.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Up to a point, yes. The argument against is obvious, of course: you train somebody and they leave, and I've seen it happen in Homs. But the alternative is a company full of people who only know what they walked in with, and that's worse for everyone including the ones who stay.", "ar": "إلى حدّ ما، نعم. الحجّة المضادّة واضحة بالطبع: تدرّب شخصاً فيرحل، وقد رأيت ذلك يحدث في حمص. لكن البديل شركة مملوءة بأشخاص لا يعرفون إلا ما دخلوا به، وهذا أسوأ للجميع بمن فيهم من يبقون.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/e12729662a8b4321.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Are some skills impossible to teach?", "ar": "هل هناك مهارات يستحيل تعليمها؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/9767af19b0c18195.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "I'd say the ones that are really judgement, yes. Take what I was describing on the Homs job. Abu Rami genuinely could not explain how he did it, and he wasn't hiding anything. You can put someone next to it for long enough that they catch it, and that's not the same as teaching it.", "ar": "أقول إن تلك التي هي حكم فعلاً، نعم. خذ ما كنت أصفه في مشروع حمص. أبو رامي لم يكن يستطيع فعلاً أن يشرح كيف يفعل ذلك، ولم يكن يخفي شيئاً. يمكنك أن تضع أحداً قريباً منه مدة طويلة حتى يلتقطه، وهذا ليس نفس تعليمه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/33be76168355ce19.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Now let's talk about education and age.", "ar": "لنتحدّث الآن عن التعليم والعمر.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/d76d7c477ad70b00.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Is it harder to learn new things as you get older?", "ar": "هل يصعب تعلّم أشياء جديدة مع التقدّم في العمر؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c6cb72b79a9fdd97.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Harder to start, I'd say, not harder to do. At thirty-one I'm better at learning something than I was at twenty at university, because I know what I don't know. What I've lost is being ready to look stupid in front of people, and honestly that's what stops me.", "ar": "أصعب أن تبدأ، على ما أعتقد، لا أصعب أن تفعل. في الحادية والثلاثين أنا أفضل في تعلّم شيء مما كنت في العشرين في الجامعة، لأنني أعرف ما لا أعرفه. ما فقدته هو أن أكون مستعداً لأن أبدو أحمق أمام الناس، وبصراحة هذا ما يوقفني.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/d542748b9fc7d44d.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you think people will need to retrain more often in the future?", "ar": "هل تعتقد أن الناس سيحتاجون إلى إعادة التدريب أكثر في المستقبل؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/d655f267c1a6b54d.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Probably, and I'd guess in my trade it will come through the materials. Everything I learned about concrete in Homs still applies. If that changes, and it might, because there's a lot of pressure on it, then half of what I know goes.", "ar": "على الأرجح، وأتوقّع أنه في مهنتي سيأتي عن طريق المواد. كل ما تعلّمته عن الخرسانة في حمص لا يزال ينطبق. إن تغيّر ذلك، وقد يتغيّر، لأن هناك ضغطاً كبيراً عليه، فسيذهب نصف ما أعرفه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/75092ceab2d83110.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "How is education in your country different from your parents' time?", "ar": "كيف يختلف التعليم في بلدك عن زمن والديك؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a7f12bd453c31ef2.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "More people get through it, I think, and it's worth less on its own. My father had a secondary certificate and that was enough to get a government job. Now everyone my age has a degree, and the degree isn't the thing that gets you hired. Who you worked for is.", "ar": "عدد من يُكملونه أكبر، على ما أعتقد، وقيمته وحده أقلّ. كان لوالدي شهادة ثانوية وكانت كافية للحصول على وظيفة حكومية. الآن كل من في عمري لديه شهادة جامعية، والشهادة ليست ما يجعلك تُعيَّن. من عملت عنده هو ما يفعل.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/abfdb1dd41866eec.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That is the end of the speaking test.", "ar": "شكراً لك. بهذا ينتهي اختبار المحادثة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f502144bdfbbc476.mp3"}], "boxes": [{"q": "Do people learn more from training courses or from experience at work?", "topic": "Learning at work", "model": "Experience, I'd say, for the kind of work I do. A course gives you the rules, which you need, and I'm not against them. But a course can't give you the feeling that something's wrong before you can say why, and on a site in Homs that feeling is most of the job.", "why": "CONTRAST"}, {"q": "Should companies be responsible for training their workers?", "topic": "Learning at work", "model": "Up to a point, yes. The argument against is obvious, of course: you train somebody and they leave, and I've seen it happen in Homs. But the alternative is a company full of people who only know what they walked in with, and that's worse for everyone including the ones who stay.", "why": "CONCEDE"}, {"q": "Are some skills impossible to teach?", "topic": "Learning at work", "model": "I'd say the ones that are really judgement, yes. Take what I was describing on the Homs job. Abu Rami genuinely could not explain how he did it, and he wasn't hiding anything. You can put someone next to it for long enough that they catch it, and that's not the same as teaching it.", "why": "EXEMPLIFY"}, {"q": "Is it harder to learn new things as you get older?", "topic": "Education and age", "model": "Harder to start, I'd say, not harder to do. At thirty-one I'm better at learning something than I was at twenty at university, because I know what I don't know. What I've lost is being ready to look stupid in front of people, and honestly that's what stops me.", "why": "QUALIFY"}, {"q": "Do you think people will need to retrain more often in the future?", "topic": "Education and age", "model": "Probably, and I'd guess in my trade it will come through the materials. Everything I learned about concrete in Homs still applies. If that changes, and it might, because there's a lot of pressure on it, then half of what I know goes.", "why": "SPECULATE"}, {"q": "How is education in your country different from your parents' time?", "topic": "Education and age", "model": "More people get through it, I think, and it's worth less on its own. My father had a secondary certificate and that was enough to get a government job. Now everyone my age has a degree, and the degree isn't the thing that gets you hired. Who you worked for is.", "why": "CONTRAST"}], "voices": {"examiner": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "candidate": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120"}});
